ect, leaving the state's partisan balance to decide the race.", "watch": "A decisive shift in the national political environment, or the emergence of state polling showing a far closer race, would be the main reasons to revisit this rating.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Arkansas leans fifteen points toward Republicans at the presidential level, and the 2028 race is open with the incumbent president term-limited. No public polls of the state, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, and neither party's nominee is settled in the available reporting, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan balance.\n\nRecent headlines show Democratic energy concentrated in the 2nd Congressional District, where polls reportedly show Chris Jones leading a Republican incumbent, but that competitiveness has not extended to statewide presidential contests. A fifteen-point Republican lean leaves Democrats needing an unusually strong national environment to put Arkansas in play. The race is rated Likely Republican, with uncertainty driven mainly by the national climate rather than anything specific to Arkansas.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0496, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0924, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0872, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0872, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0887, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0862, "margin": -15.0}]}